{"id": "q0043", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1444618742, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "John decides to take up an odd hobby of speed talking.  His normally speaking speed is 150 WPM.  After training his speed is 2.5 times faster than his starting speed.  How long would it take him to speak 10 pages if each page has 450 words per page?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0043.wav", "input_sha256": "7511979c576dfe6b7baf56db69b2a66a2b5852357ac54a1a34eb69f2c68bb239", "input_samples": 320200, "input_s": 20.012, "n_real_chunks": 21, "score": 0.2395, "act": 0.9986, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so John's starting speed is 150 words per minute. After training, his speed is 2. 5 times faster, so that would be 15 0 times 2.5, which is 3 75 words per minute. Each page has 4 50 words, and he needs to speak 10 pages, so that's 45 0 times 1 0, which is 4, 50 0 words total. To find the time, divide the total words by his speaking speed: 4, 5 00 divided by 3 75. Let' s see, 3 7 5 goes into 4,5 00 about 1 2 times. So it would take him 12 minutes to speak 1 0 pages at his new speed.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 20, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 39, "feed_lag_max_ms": 11015, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 223683, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0043_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "97c7eca810d