{"id": "q0075", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2488653568, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "Jake is shopping at a clothing store. The store has a buy one get one 50% off deal on T-shirts. Jake buys 2 T-shirts. The original price of each T-shirt is $8. Then, Jake buys a pair of shoes that is 40% off the original price. The original price of the shoes is $40. What is the total amount of money Jake spends at the store?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0075.wav", "input_sha256": "718c9f89dcc1b4e187100e0c799efedf8266ac17af8f537da6046267348e8a40", "input_samples": 401600, "input_s": 25.1, "n_real_chunks": 26, "score": 0.2791, "act": 0.9995, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Jake buys two T-shirt s at $8 each. The store has a buy one get one 5 0% off deal, so he pays full price for the first one and half price for the second. That' s $8 plus $4, which is $1 2 for the T-shirts. Then, the shoes are 40% off. So he pays 60% of $40, which is $24. Adding the T-shirts and the shoes, $12 plus $ 24 equal s $3 6. So the total amount Jake spends is 3 6.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 25, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 28, "feed_lag_max_ms": 7448, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 111634, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0075_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "60116be422551f6460c470fd991b2b02b051470da3fb595c6b8a19