{"id": "q0097", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3839400866, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "Mark's car breaks down and he needs to get a new radiator.  The cost for a new radiator is $400 but he goes to get it at a junk shop and gets it for 80% off.  He then hires a mechanic to install it and it takes 3 hours at $50 an hour.  How much did he pay?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0097.wav", "input_sha256": "45f43b7c397a695e39ba151b7ea0f7ae6a02665a18d449d0a28dcc09674722ed", "input_samples": 332200, "input_s": 20.762, "n_real_chunks": 21, "score": 0.1464, "act": 0.9994, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "The cost of the ra diator was $40 0, but he got it for 80% off. So, let's calculate that first. 80% off means he paid 2 0% of the original price. 2 0% of 400 is 0. 2 times 400, which is 80 dollars. Then, the mechanic charged him 5 0 dollars per hour for three hours. That' s 5 0 times 3, which is 1 50 dollars. Now, add ing both amounts together: 80 plus 150 equal s 2 30 dollars. So Mark paid a total of 2 30 dollars.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 20, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 39, "feed_lag_max_ms": 9573, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 188060, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0097_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "06f70993be0506ff9d26ecfbc0cbf0a8ac0c30d3442253915f8bbead92766858", "sr": 24000,