{"id": "q0425", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3995831193, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "Provide a bulleted list of things to think about when buying a house", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0425.wav", "input_sha256": "9e6324dca26b1ad3031b2273503cffcd44dcf8caad3c270cbc37b8ffa7bf4a9d", "input_samples": 62400, "input_s": 3.9, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.488, "act": 0.9959, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So, here are some things to think about when buying a house. First, make sure you know what your budget is before you start looking for homes. You don' t want to get caught up in the excitement of finding the perfect place and then realize it's out of your price range. Second, consider location. Think about how close you'll be to work, schools, grocery stores, parks, and other amenities that matter to you. Third, check the neighborhood. Do some research on crime rates, school quality, and local property values. Fourth, look at the condition of the house. Have an expert inspect it for any hidden issues like termite damage or roof problems. Fifth, think about long-term plans. Will this home still fit your needs in five or ten years? Finally, don't forget to factor in closing costs, property taxes, and maintenance expenses. They can add up quickly.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 4, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 43, "feed_lag_max_ms": 11037, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 220701,